hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"44101","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Nafi, that Abdullah ibn Umar did not pray on the day of Fitr before the prayer or after it."
"44102","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Sa'id from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Salih ibn Khawwat that Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah informed him: The prayer of fear (Salat al-Khawf) is that the Imam stands with a group of his companions while another group faces the enemy. The Imam bows one rak'ah and prostrates with those who are with him. Then he stands, and when he is fully standing upright, they complete the remaining rak'ah for themselves. Then they give the taslim and depart, while the Imam remains standing. Thus they become the ones facing the enemy. Then the others who have not yet prayed come forward, say the takbir behind the Imam, and he bows with them for the rak'ah and prostrates. Then he gives the taslim, and they stand and complete the remaining rak'ah for themselves, then give the taslim."
"44201","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Salih ibn Khawwat that Sahl ibn Abi Hathma related to him that the form of the prayer of fear was that the imam stood with a group of his companions"
"44202","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Salih ibn Khawwat that Sahl ibn Abi Hathma related to him that the form of the prayer of fear was that the imam stood with a group of his companions"
"44301","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar"
"44302","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar"
"44401","And it was narrated to me from Malik, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, that he used to pray on the Day of Fitr before the prayer in the Masjid."
"44402","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwah from his father from Aisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that she said: The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led the people in prayer. He stood and prolonged the standing, then bowed and prolonged the bowing, then stood and prolonged the standing, though it was shorter than the first standing, then bowed and prolonged the bowing, though it was shorter than the first bowing, then raised his head and prostrated. Then he did in the second rak'ah the like of that. Then he departed, and the sun had become clear. He addressed the people, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: ""The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah; they do not eclipse for the death of anyone nor for his life. So when you see that, supplicate Allah, say the takbir, and give charity."" Then he said: ""O community of Muhammad! By Allah, there is no one more jealous than Allah, Mighty and Majestic, that His male servant should commit fornication or His female servant commit fornication. O community of Muhammad! By Allah, if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."""
